---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Sheet from '../layouts/Sheet.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
import '../styles/home.css';   // the same rows and the same card treatment as the index
import '../styles/about.css';
import portrait from '../assets/img/about-portrait.png';
import sketch1 from '../assets/img/about-sketch-1.png';
import sketch2 from '../assets/img/about-sketch-2.png';
import studio1 from '../assets/img/about-studio-1.png';
import studio2 from '../assets/img/about-studio-2.png';
import home1 from '../assets/img/about-home-1.png';
import home2 from '../assets/img/about-home-2.png';
import michigan from '../assets/img/about-michigan.jpg';

// The same eight pictures the Webflow About page used, framed like the project cards on the index:
// 24px radius, no hairline, the image covering the frame, every frame 3:2. The portrait is the
// hero's figure, cropped half-length with the figure on the left third. Each chapter is the index's
// row — the years at column 1, the words on the reading column from 6 — and carries its pictures
// beneath the words as the cards do: a pair of halves after each paragraph that has one, or a
// single under the words. No hairline in the body: sections are parted by air.
const hero = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [720, 1100, 1600, 2036], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 164vw, (max-width: 1440px) 151vw, 2041px', loading: 'eager' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };
const half = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [480, 720, 1100, 1440], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 45vw, 612px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };
const single = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [720, 1100, 1440], sizes: '(max-width: 1023px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 53vw, 718px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };

// The work the story names, where the index already links it.
const curio = 'https://www.figma.com/design/BiXcn2d7kNwzXtuw1aUGDx/Curio-Work?node-id=0-1';
const droploft = 'https://www.figma.com/design/3nUKfaJoAkZQdlZwzpyFff/Dify-Demos?node-id=0-1';
const observe = 'https://github.com/KyleXu0420/observe';
const echo = 'https://doi.org/10.7302/29019';

const facts = [
  { label: 'Worked with', items: ['Temper', 'Dify (LangGenius)', 'Curio Digital Therapeutics', 'Infloww', 'Heygen', 'Eaton Corporation', 'HIL Architects'] },
  { label: 'Earlier', items: ['ColdMe (co-founder, 2021)', 'COIL Connect for Virtual Exchange', 'Capital Area District Libraries', 'Erb Family Foundation'] },
  { label: 'Studied at', lines: true, items: ['M.S. Information (HCI), University of Michigan, 2022–2025', "B.Eng. Architecture, Xi'an University of Architecture and Technology, 2016–2022"] },
  { label: 'Skills', items: ['AI UX', 'Agent workflows', 'Information architecture', 'Product strategy', 'Design systems', 'UX research', 'Usability testing', 'Frontend prototyping', 'Design-to-code'] },
  { label: 'Tools', items: ['Figma', 'React', 'TypeScript', 'Tailwind', 'Claude Code', 'Cursor', 'Codex', 'Python'] },
  { label: 'Languages', items: ['English', 'Mandarin (native)'] },
];
---
<Sheet
  title="About — Kyle Xu"
  description="Kyle Xu, AI product designer. Six years of architecture, then HCI at the University of Michigan; since 2022 at Eaton, Heygen, Infloww, Curio Digital Therapeutics, Dify and Temper."
  ogImage="/og-about.jpg"
>
  <section class="col hero" aria-labelledby="h1">
    <h1 class="display claim" id="h1">I trained as an architect for six years before I moved to AI products.</h1>
    <p class="lead deck">At fifteen I was already sketching buildings instead of studying for the gaokao.</p>
    <div class="photo portrait"><Picture src={portrait} {...hero} alt="Kyle in kendo uniform, holding a helmet, in front of a wall of labelled equipment shelves" /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="Organisations, skills, tools and languages">
    <dl class="facts">
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="meta">{f.label}</dt>
          <dd>{f.lines
            ? f.items.map((it) => <span class="line">{it}</span>)
            : f.items.map((it, i) => <><span class="nb">{it}{i < f.items.length - 1 && ','}</span>{i < f.items.length - 1 && ' '}</>)}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="How I got here">
    <ul class="tl story">
      <li>
        <span class="when">2013 – 2019</span>
        <div class="what">
          <p>Alongside the sketches I was in volunteer building workshops in Hangzhou. By 2017 I was being paid to design spaces and art pieces for my father's business associates. At eighteen a local design studio took me on for my first professional project. In 2016 I got into architecture school in Xi'an.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={sketch1} {...half} alt="Kyle as a student, sitting on the steps of a rooftop garden" /></div>
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={sketch2} {...half} alt="Kyle's reflection in the window of a brick building, camera raised" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <p>In 2019 I went <span class="nb">part-time</span> at HIL Architects, as a junior architect and a teaching assistant. I learned there that cost and construction decide more of a building than the drawing does. The title didn't get me much on its own, so I kept finding my own clients through school.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={studio1} {...half} alt="A small studio interior: a long wooden table and a glass partition" /></div>
          <div class="photo right"><Picture src={studio2} {...half} alt="A narrow city street lined with shop signs" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="when">2020 – 2022</span>
        <div class="what">
          <p>The pandemic kept me at home for most of those three years, working on UI and UX projects with partners in a few Chinese cities. One was a WeChat <span class="nb">mini-program</span> for a neighbourhood in Xi'an's Muslim Quarter, a project my university ran with the city. In 2021 I co-founded ColdMe as its designer, and with a few people from a film community I built and launched an app. I finished the B.Eng. in 2022.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo up"><Picture src={home1} {...half} alt="Kyle at a workbench in a workshop" /></div>
          <div class="photo mid"><Picture src={home2} {...half} alt="A night-market kitchen in Xi'an's Muslim Quarter, cooks at the grills" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="when">2022 – now</span>
        <div class="what">
          <p>From then on all of the work was on screens. In the summer of 2022 I interned at Eaton on an <a class="ref" href={href('/projects/eaton')}>IoT configuration tool</a> for airport clients, then started the master's in HCI at the University of Michigan. The next summer, at Heygen, I <span class="nb">re-architected</span> <a class="ref" href={href('/projects/heygen')}>the AI video editor</a> around the script.</p>
          <p>My thesis, <a class="ref" href={echo} rel="noopener">Echo</a>, was an <span class="nb">LLM-driven</span> <span class="nb">future-self</span> avatar for everyday health habits. I piloted it with 8 people over 16 days, then ran a <span class="nb">12-day</span> deployment with 36. I finished the degree in 2025.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={michigan} {...single} alt="Kyle with classmates at the University of Michigan" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <p>In 2024, at Infloww, the product was a chat assistant for a B2B CRM, and most of the design turned out to be the work around the model. With the prompt engineers I designed the payment and messaging tools for the cases where it's wrong.</p>
          <p>From late 2024 I was the founding product designer at Curio Digital Therapeutics, on <a class="ref" href={curio} rel="noopener">MamaLift and MenoLift</a>, two <span class="nb">FDA-cleared</span> products. The design system, the information architecture and a feature called the Achievement Garden all went through clinical review.</p>
          <p>In 2026 I joined Dify, an AI application platform, as their AI product designer. I designed <a class="ref" href={droploft} rel="noopener">Droploft</a>, a team knowledge base; Syncless, a <span class="nb">multi-agent</span> workplace concept; and the Dify Enterprise main app. After that I spent three months on contract at Temper, inside the production codebase, on the <span class="nb">design-token</span> architecture and <a class="ref" href={observe} rel="noopener">the lint checkers</a> that enforce it.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="signoff">
    <p class="stance">I'm most useful once the model works and before the interface is settled.</p>
    <p>That's the stretch where the product decides what the agent may do and where a person can stop it. I've done it at Infloww and at Dify. If that's where your product is, <a class="ref" href="mailto:kylexu@umich.edu">write to me</a>.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Sheet>
